(a) License, permit and administrative fees applicable to this division are set out as follows:
(1) Malt beverages, distilled spirits and wine to be served by the drink for consumption only on the premises: $1,500.00 per year;
(2) Retail package of distilled spirits: $2,000.00 per year;
(3) Retail package of malt beverage and wine: $1,500.00 per year;
(4) Malt beverage and wine catering off-premises: $2,000.00 per year;
(5) Catering event permit fee (if caterer is domiciled): $25.00 per event;
(6) Catering event permit fee (if caterer is non-domiciled): $50.00 per event;
(7) Transfer fee: one-half of the annual license fee for the license to be transferred;
(8) Employee pouring-permit fee: $30.00 per year;
(9) Application fee: $300.00.
(b) Each applicant for a license shall pay an application fee to the city according to its published schedule of fees.
(c) Maximum number of distilled spirits retail licenses permitted.
(1) Subject to subsections (2)—(5) below, the city will not accept any applications for the retail sale of distilled spirits by the package, and no licenses for the retail sale of distilled spirits by the package shall be issued over the number of two.
(2) If at any time and for whatever reason, the number of active licenses for the retail sale of distilled spirits by the package falls below two, then the city shall accept applications for and issue such additional licenses for the retail sale of distilled spirits by the package so as to bring the total number of licenses for the retail sale of distilled spirits by the package to two.
(3) The provisions of subsection (2) notwithstanding, one additional license may be issued once the population of the city exceeds 20,000. Additional licenses may be issued in the future for each 10,000 person increase in population over 20,000 in determining population, the city shall utilize the most recent population figures published by the Atlanta Regional Commission. In absence of such figures, the city may utilize the United States Census.
(4) If the total number of permitted licenses has increased pursuant to subsection (3) above, and if at any time, the number of licenses for retail sale of distilled spirits by the package falls below the permitted number, then the city may accept applications for and issue such additional licenses for the retail sale of distilled spirits by the package so as to bring the total number of licenses for retail sale of distilled spirits by the package to the total number then permitted.
(5) If the city receives more qualified applications than the allotted licenses to be issued under this section, then the selection of the successful application shall be conducted by a lottery system overseen by an independent third-party accounting firm. The applications drawn from the lottery system shall be presented to the city council for action on the approval of the licenses to be issued.
(Code 2010, § 7-3-5; Ord. of 4-9-2009; Ord. of 9-8-2022(2))
State Law reference— License fees, O.C.G.A. §§ 3-4-50, 3-4-110, 3-5-43,

